                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Analyse the training examples:\n\n1. In each example, there is an outer bounding shape (diamond or rectangle) and an inner block of a different color.\n2. The inner block projects horizontally and vertically (like a cross or raycast) until it hits the boundary of the enclosing shape.\n   - Example 1: Inner block is 3x3 of color 3. Enclosing shape is a diamond of color 7. The rows and columns corresponding to the 3x3 block are filled with 3 inside the diamond.\n   - Example 2: Inner block is 3x3 of color 8. Enclosing shape is a rectangle of color 1. The horizontal rows (rows 3,4,5) and vertical columns (cols 8,9,10) extend to the rectangle boundary. Rows 3,4,5 are filled across columns 6 to 11 (inside the rectangle). Col 8,9,10 are extended to row 2 and 6.\n   - Example 3: Inner block is 2x2 of color 1. It extends horizontally (rows 6, 7 across to diamond boundaries) and vertically (cols 6, 7 up and down until they hit diamond boundary 7).\n\nSo the inner block's rows and columns are projected horizontally and vertically, filling with the inner block's color, up to (but not through or overwriting) the boundary shape.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid!",
